Two files are below. I left out both operations requests. The node's authority is only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`, so it has no interface for writing `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or calling `https://metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would need new capabilities in the node's `with` clause, and those would have to be granted in the graph.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let knowledge = crate::aap::caps::kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

